Fix this in ui.html (pageAgent) by detecting the floats themselves; don't infer them from line-rect edges.

1. Add a helper that finds floats intruding into the element's lines:
```js
function floatInset(el, box, top, bottom) {
  let l = box.x, r = box.x + box.w, covered = true;
  // Floats that come before el (as siblings of el or of an ancestor) in the same block formatting context
  for (let a = el; a && a !== S.doc.body; a = a.parentElement) {
    const pc = a.parentElement && css(a.parentElement);
    if (pc && /flex|grid/.test(pc.display)) break;          // floats don't apply in flex/grid
    for (let n = a.previousElementSibling; n; n = n.previousElementSibling) {
      const c = css(n);
      if (c.float === 'none' || c.position === 'absolute' || c.position === 'fixed') continue;
      const fr = n.getBoundingClientRect(), m = (p) => parseFloat(c[p]) || 0;
      const ft = fr.top - m('marginTop'), fb = fr.bottom + m('marginBottom');
      if (fb <= top + 1 || ft >= bottom - 1) continue;      // no vertical overlap
      if (fb < bottom - 1) covered = false;                 // float ends partway through the text
      if (c.float === 'left' || c.float === 'inline-start') l = Math.max(l, fr.right + m('marginRight'));
      else r = Math.min(r, fr.left - m('marginLeft'));
    }
    const ac = css(a);
    if (a !== el && (ac.overflow !== 'visible' || ac.display === 'flow-root' || ac.display === 'inline-block')) break; // stop at the BFC root
  }
  return { x: l, w: r - l, covered };
}
```

2. In `textGeometry()`, in the `lines.length > 1` branch, compute `const box0 = wrapBox || {x:L, w:R-L}`. If `target` is an element (for a text node, use its parent), call `const fi = floatInset(el, box0, T, B)`.
   - If `fi.w < box0.w - 1` and `fi.covered` is true, use `{x: fi.x, w: fi.w}` as the box. Keep `align` and `autoResize: 'HEIGHT'`.
   - If the float ends partway through the text (`!fi.covered`), keep the current behaviour. Optionally, split the text into two TEXT nodes at the first line whose top is at or below the float's bottom. Get the character offset from `S.doc.caretRangeFromPoint(lineLeft + 1, lineMid)`, then map it to a segment index. The upper node uses the inset box and the lower node uses the full box.

   Apply the same check to the single-line `alignBox` path (narrow the alignBox the same way) so centred or right-aligned single lines next to a float are still detected correctly.

3. `looseText()` gets the fix automatically because it uses the same `textGeometry`.

**Effect.** A paragraph whose box is already a BFC (overflow:hidden, flow-root or a flex item) sits beside the float, so the inset never exceeds its content box and nothing changes. Once the text stops overlapping the image, the existing Auto Layout detection may produce a HORIZONTAL [img, text] row on its own; no special-case row building is needed. Only standard Figma properties (x, width, textAutoResize HEIGHT) are involved.
